# Servabo — Frontend Client Environment Variables Template
# Copy this file locally to '.env' and configure according to target host conditions.

# 1. API Gateway Target Context
# Leave VITE_API_URL UNSET here (ARCH-30 Tranche 1). Development defaults to
# http://localhost:8000/api/v1 and production to same-origin /api/v1. Vite reads
# .env for `vite build` too, and vite.config.ts refuses a production build with
# an absolute URL. For a non-default dev port use .env.development.local, which
# start_dev.ps1 and start_dev.sh write for you.
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1

# 2. The public website (website session). Pricing and the legal pages live there;
# the app's /pricing, /terms and /privacy send people to it. Development defaults
# to http://localhost:4321 (start_dev.sh --website), production to
# https://servabo.app. Set it for the fallback domain or a preview deployment.
# VITE_WEBSITE_URL=https://servabo.app

# 3. Error tracking (Final session 1). Empty = off: no SDK is loaded and nothing is sent. The DSN of the web app's own
# Sentry (EU region) or GlitchTip project; baked in when the bundle is built. The ingest host must also be allowed by the
# Content-Security-Policy: set SENTRY_INGEST_HOST (see docs/RUNBOOK.md 9.13; `python scripts/preflight.py` prints it).
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
# VITE_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# VITE_RELEASE=
# VITE_SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0

# Those are the only variables the web app reads (src/services/api/client.ts,
# src/config/website.ts, src/monitoring.ts).
# F-010: the template used to list VITE_APP_NAME, VITE_APP_VERSION and
# VITE_ENVIRONMENT, which nothing reads; they were removed so a value set here
# is never silently ignored. Branding (name, colours, logo) comes from the
# server's branding manifest, not from build-time variables.
